Every third-party licence in this repository is permissive. There is no
copyleft component: the AGPL-3.0 test fixtures that OpenZeppelin vendors for
its own test suite (halmos-cheatcodes, erc4626-tests) were removed, because
nothing here imported them and redistributing strong-copyleft code that serves
no purpose is a liability with no upside.

The dependencies are vendored rather than referenced as git submodules, so a
clone gets a complete, buildable tree with no `--recursive` step. What is
vendored is only what TraderMarket compiles and tests against: upstream test
suites, documentation and build scripts are not included.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
JAVASCRIPT DEPENDENCIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`services/live-room/` and `prototype/live-market-app/` declare dependencies in
`package.json` and do not vendor `node_modules/`. Nothing third-party is
redistributed here; consumers install those packages themselves under the
publishers' own terms.

For the live inventory, run `npm ls --all` in either package. This file does
not duplicate it, because a hand-copied dependency list goes stale silently
and a stale licence inventory is worse than none.

